<main class="main"><div class="container">




<header class="jumbotron">
	<h1>The World Is Your CI (beta)</h1>
	<p><strong>wiyci</strong> aggregates downstream build logs of Free and Open Source software projects and presents them as a typical Continuous Integration platform would, highlighting compiler warnings and failed tests. We hope to increase upstream awareness of downstream build problems and encourage the community to contribute fixes.</p>
	<p><strong>wiyci</strong> currently sources build logs from <strong>Alpine</strong>, <strong>Fedora</strong>, <strong>Nix</strong>, and <strong>FreeBSD</strong>, covering a variety of kernels (<strong>Linux</strong>, <strong>FreeBSD</strong>, <strong>Darwin</strong>), system libraries (<strong>glibc</strong>, <strong>musl</strong>, <strong>FreeBSD libc</strong>, <strong>Apple libc</strong>), hardware architectures (<strong>x86_64</strong>, <strong>x86</strong>, <strong>arm</strong>, <strong>aarch64</strong>, <strong>loongarch64</strong>, <strong>ppc64</strong>, <strong>riscv64</strong>, <strong>s390x</strong>), and numerous toolchains.</p>
	<p>Feel free to suggest more <a href="https://github.com/AMDmi3/wiyci/issues/31">build log sources</a>, more <a href="https://github.com/AMDmi3/wiyci/issues/14">facts to parse</a>, or projects not yet covered that you're interested in.</p>
</header>

